				1731,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Finalize CreateEffectForRequest parameter borrowing in utility and dispatcher\n\nUpdate parameter utility functions in Params.rs to accept `&Value` instead of `Value`, moving necessary clone operations inside the function bodies. Update the central dispatcher Try macro in mod.rs to pass `&Parameters` to CreateEffect constructors instead of cloning the owned value unconditionally.\n\nThis completes the parameter borrowing refactor that reduces clone overhead on the hot dispatch path across all CreateEffectForRequest layers.",
			"SHA": "9c2c3857a8f3aa0557286314607a3c2191be2528"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-04T19:14:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Finalize CreateEffectForRequest string matching simplification\n\nComplete the CreateEffectForRequest dispatch refactoring by converting the remaining two modules from macro-generated patterns to explicit string predicates.\n\nLanguageFeatures.rs replaces its match expression with `MethodName.starts_with(\"register_\") && MethodName.ends_with(\"_provider\")` and removes a stray extra brace left over from macro expansion. WindowUI.rs replaces the catch-all wildcard match with `MethodName.starts_with(\"Window.\")` plus a descriptive comment, ensuring only Window-namespace methods route here.\n\nAll CreateEffectForRequest modules now use explicit, self-documenting dispatch predicates instead of macro-generated tokens.",
			"SHA": "bc05e8208557e6236d112704752939fa17599dc3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-04T19:14:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				25
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Simplify CreateEffectForRequest string matching\n\nReplace macro-generated match expressions and identifier constants with explicit string literal comparisons and `starts_with`/`ends_with` predicates across all CreateEffectForRequest modules. Static method names now use direct string matching (\"Authentication.GetSession\" | \"Authentication.GetAccounts\") instead of inferred identifier constants. Dynamic command patterns collapse into concise boolean expressions — `$gitExec` and `$terminal:` families use `MethodName.starts_with(...)`, `register_*_provider` uses a start+end check, and `$scm:`, `$statusBar:`, `$webview:`, and `tree.` prefixes follow the same pattern.\n\nThis removes macro coupling from the dispatch predicates, makes accepted method names immediately visible in each file, and eliminates stale `std::sync::Arc` imports left over from macro expansion. The central dispatcher now routes through cleaner pre-filters that operate on concrete strings rather than generated tokens.",
			"SHA": "cafbc510d7e2b33f142fd0badacefb43068381ff"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-04T19:09:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				28
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Add Matches pre-filter and borrow Parameters in CreateEffectForRequest\n\nIntroduce a `Matches(MethodName: &str) -> bool` predicate on every CreateEffectForRequest module so the central dispatcher can reject non-matching method names before invoking the full constructor. This eliminates unnecessary work and aligns with the ActionEffect dispatch pattern used elsewhere.\n\nChange `CreateEffect` signatures across all modules from `Parameters: Value` to `Parameters: &Value`, removing the unconditional `Parameters.clone()` call from the hot dispatch path and deferring cloning into the individual effect macro invocations only when needed.\n\nReorder the module chain in `Source/Track/Effect/CreateEffectForRequest/mod.rs` — moving `FileSystem`, `Commands`, `Terminal`, and `TreeView` into a new sequence — and wrap each `Try!` invocation with the `Matches` guard.",
			"SHA": "be9aaf5b1cc0156d3236573d11a617984e0da2ef"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-04T19:06:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Clean up ActiveOperations registry on RPC cancellation\n\nImmediately remove the cancelled operation from the ActiveOperations write lock after triggering its cancellation token, preventing a leaked CancellationToken per RPC that accumulated when operations did not reach their own UnregisterOperation call site.\n\nRemove the redundant client-side method name format check that rejected paths containing \"../\" or \"::\" separators from the request validation path.",
			"SHA": "28bf3528fd4eb3af543c2ef45b1a37c622cd6088"
		}
	],
